{"availability":"available","full":"alexprengere/python_playground","name":"python_playground","description":"Leverage Ace and Pyodide to have a pure JS python playground","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":9,"forks":3,"created":"2025-06-29T08:51:16Z","updated":"2025-07-01T12:37:18Z","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":[],"demo":"https://pyodide.org/en/stable/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:31:16.307Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:31:16.307Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:31:16.307Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T16:22:58.614Z","stars":9,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-04T16:45:05.514Z","stars":9,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-06T17:13:18.032Z","stars":9,"forks":3},{"at":"2026-10-08T22:31:16.307Z","stars":9,"forks":3}],"technologies":[],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T09:39:49.662Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This shows that you can run a Python interpreter in the browser using Pyodide. In one sentence, Pyodide is a Python distribution for the browser (and Node.js), based on WebAssembly. Here it is paired with the Ace code editor, which is a lightweight, embeddable code editor written in JavaScript.","You can leverage micropip to install dependencies. For the dependencies that are pure-Python, the wheels are fetched from PyPI, and for the other ones, thankfully, the Pyodide team has already built WASM wheels for them.","In this UI you can upload files, it will use pyodide.FS.writeFile(...), which writes those files to the virtual filesystem of Pyodide. Note that any code written in the editor will be saved to the browser local storage, so you can come back later and continue working on it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/alexprengere/python_playground/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"0d52e3502a6763d20ec3ed6cc784c0e1f89d5e62e9d62d9b9bda0d1e3c693fb6","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:16:08.670Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T19:04:45.166Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2025-07-0